      "chunkIndex": 3,
      "contentPreview": "THE REAL DEFECT UNDERNEATH H1 IS AN UNSTATED INVARIANT, not a missing compile-time gate. All three defaults depend on: ListScoped(null) returns the COMPLETE cross-scope listing. That is precisely what HttpMemoryStore.ListScoped violated (no limit sent, server defaults to 200 rows). The fix that prevents recurrence is to write the invariant onto IMemoryStore.ListScoped and test it, not to delete members. When a review proposes compile-time forcing, check first whether the members actually differ",
